{"seq":4,"slug":"human-centered-design","title":"以人为中心设计","stage":"DONE","category":"design-thinking","chapterCount":3,"docCount":11,"url":"/h/design-thinking/human-centered-design","rating":{"composite":3.56,"verdict":"stable","groups":{"quality":4,"coverage":3.25,"positioning":4,"strategic":3},"weights":{"quality":0.3,"coverage":0.25,"positioning":0.2,"strategic":0.25},"profile":{"composite":3.42,"verdict":"neutral","uScore":3.25}},"introMarkdown":"# 以人为中心设计 简介\n\n以人为中心的设计是一种将用户的需求、能力和行为置于设计过程核心位置的方法论。它强调设计不是设计师的自我表达，而是为真实的人解决真实问题的过程。从 ISO 9241-210 标准的制定到 IDEO 的人本设计实践，这一理念已经成为当代设计领域的共识性原则。\n\n本知识库面向希望深入理解和实践以人为中心设计方法的学习者，无论你是用户体验设计师、产品经理、服务设计师还是关注用户需求的工程师，都能在这里找到系统的方法论和实践指导。\n\n全书共分为三章，从用户需求的深入分析出发，拓展到面向所有人的包容性设计理念，最终深入到让用户参与设计过程的参与式方法。\n\n第一章**用户需求分析**介绍理解用户真实需求的深层方法，涵盖需求层次理论、情境调查技术、利益相关者映射以及待完成任务框架，帮助你超越表面需求发现用户的深层动机。\n\n第二章**包容性设计**探讨如何设计能够被最广泛人群使用的产品和服务，涵盖无障碍原则、通用设计理念以及面向多样性群体的设计方法，帮助你在设计中体现对每一位用户的尊重和关怀。\n\n第三章**参与式设计**讲解如何让用户和利益相关者直接参与到设计过程中来，涵盖共创方法、社区参与策略、设计工作坊的组织以及参与式评估方法，帮助你将\"为用户设计\"升级为\"与用户一起设计\"。\n\n推荐学习路径为先通过第一章掌握需求分析的深层方法，再通过第二章拓展设计视野关注更广泛的用户群体，最后通过第三章学会让用户成为设计过程的共同参与者。建议在学习过程中反思自己过往项目中的用户研究实践，寻找改进空间。\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"user-needs-analysis","title":"用户需求分析","docCount":4,"url":"/h/design-thinking/human-centered-design/user-needs-analysis","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"needs-hierarchy","title":"需求层次与优先级分析","url":"/h/design-thinking/human-centered-design/user-needs-analysis/needs-hierarchy"},{"seq":2,"slug":"contextual-inquiry","title":"情境调研与田野观察","url":"/h/design-thinking/human-centered-design/user-needs-analysis/contextual-inquiry"},{"seq":3,"slug":"stakeholder-mapping","title":"利益相关者地图","url":"/h/design-thinking/human-centered-design/user-needs-analysis/stakeholder-mapping"},{"seq":4,"slug":"jobs-to-be-done","title":"JTBD 框架与需求本质","url":"/h/design-thinking/human-centered-design/user-needs-analysis/jobs-to-be-done"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"inclusive-design","title":"包容性设计","docCount":3,"url":"/h/design-thinking/human-centered-design/inclusive-design","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"accessibility-principles","title":"无障碍设计原则","url":"/h/design-thinking/human-centered-design/inclusive-design/accessibility-principles"},{"seq":2,"slug":"universal-design","title":"通用设计七原则","url":"/h/design-thinking/human-centered-design/inclusive-design/universal-design"},{"seq":3,"slug":"designing-for-diversity","title":"多样性设计与文化包容","url":"/h/design-thinking/human-centered-design/inclusive-design/designing-for-diversity"}]},{"seq":3,"slug":"participatory-design","title":"参与式设计","docCount":4,"url":"/h/design-thinking/human-centered-design/participatory-design","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"co-design-methods","title":"共创设计方法","url":"/h/design-thinking/human-centered-design/participatory-design/co-design-methods"},{"seq":2,"slug":"community-engagement","title":"社区参与与利益共同体","url":"/h/design-thinking/human-centered-design/participatory-design/community-engagement"},{"seq":3,"slug":"design-workshops","title":"设计工作坊引导","url":"/h/design-thinking/human-centered-design/participatory-design/design-workshops"},{"seq":4,"slug":"participatory-evaluation","title":"参与式评估与反馈","url":"/h/design-thinking/human-centered-design/participatory-design/participatory-evaluation"}]}]}